From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:27:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/26] [Diffusion] Causal Wan: cache-aware cross-attention in
 the stock block

CausalWanTransformerBlock.forward passes crossattn_cache to self.attn2, but
e00930c built attn2 as WanT2VCrossAttention, whose forward(x, context,
context_lens) has no such argument: the stock causal-Wan block raised a
TypeError on its first forward. attn2 is now CausalWanT2VCrossAttention, a
WanT2VCrossAttention subclass (same parameters and weight names) that stores
the projected/normalized text K/V in the block's CrossAttentionKVCache on the
first call after a reset and reuses them afterwards (the math of LongLive2's
_cross_attn_with_cache); without a cache it is exactly the parent forward.
LongLive2 blocks call their own _cross_attn_with_cache and are unaffected.

Tests: cached == uncached output, one context projection per cache epoch,
reset re-projects, no-cache path identical to WanT2VCrossAttention.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
